{
 "title": "Paycheck",
 "note": "Voice-over assembled from Coworker Retiring (0-35.6s) and Retirement Scenes (126.7-133.7s); times are on the final video timeline.",
 "text": "So I had a conversation with an old employee of mine, and guess what? He's about to retire soon. Or at least he thinks. It's my job to figure out and help him see if he's gonna retire. We took the money in his old 401k that he left sitting at his old job, and we're gonna roll that into a private pension that's gonna produce a certain amount of money for him. And then we're gonna add up his social security, we're gonna take that total, and subtract it by the monthly expenses. And guess what? If there's a positive number, he can retire today. If there's a negative number, we have to work on a solution to fix that balance. It's really that simple. This is my job, this is what I do for people every single day. If you're within 10 years of retirement or are already there, DM me the word INCOME, and I'll stress test your plan.",
